WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:03.730
<b>Dear Yokomizo-dono</b>

00:00.910 --> 00:03.720
<i>Dear Yokomizo-dono,</i>

00:04.050 --> 00:06.340
<i>How is it in the afterlife?</i>

00:06.930 --> 00:11.110
<i>Knowing you, I suspect 
you're looking for ways</i>

00:11.110 --> 00:14.350
<i>to manipulate divine powers 
into allowing you an escape.</i>

00:14.350 --> 00:19.480
<i>I bet you're jealous of my 
lavish lifestyle right now.</i>

00:19.950 --> 00:21.480
<i>No, I'm not lying.</i>

00:21.480 --> 00:23.770
<i>The meals are extravagant and exquisite.</i>

00:23.770 --> 00:24.620
Meal time!

00:28.960 --> 00:30.460
Thank you.

00:30.460 --> 00:32.830
<i>And even the Celtic god Ruad Rofhessa</i>

00:32.830 --> 00:35.340
<i>would envy the freedom afforded 
to me during my reading times.</i>

00:35.950 --> 00:37.200
You, guard.

00:38.190 --> 00:40.310
I wish to read books on occultism.

00:40.310 --> 00:41.300
Take me to the library.

00:41.540 --> 00:43.300
You aren't allowed to leave.

00:43.300 --> 00:45.180
At least lend me a book, then.

00:47.360 --> 00:51.720
If the rinse cycle does not occur 
during the washing process, see page 8.

00:52.880 --> 00:55.710
<i>I get to read books that 
I rarely do otherwise.</i>

00:57.520 --> 01:00.200
<i>I never even think about the fact</i>

01:00.590 --> 01:03.430
<i>that you no longer exist in this world.</i>

01:20.990 --> 01:22.510
<i>Oh, Yokomizo...</i>

01:22.710 --> 01:24.410
<i>Unlike the fool that you are,</i>

01:22.900 --> 01:24.390
Infiltration successful.

01:24.390 --> 01:25.200
Ow, ow, ow...

01:24.410 --> 01:28.370
<i>I am able to maintain my composure 
and grace during this crisis.</i>

01:25.200 --> 01:26.070
Are you all right?

01:26.070 --> 01:27.360
I think so.

01:28.370 --> 01:33.980
Sech stempel schrecken 
geht durch mein gebein!

01:36.100 --> 01:39.010
Um... We're the Armed Detective Agency.

01:39.700 --> 01:41.490
We're here to help you.

03:16.650 --> 03:20.130
The Detective Agency's been framed 
by the Decay of Angels.

03:20.740 --> 03:25.040
You were captured by the enemy 
trying to warn us about their trap.

03:25.620 --> 03:30.580
We used the Eyes of God to find you 
here so that we can get you out.

03:31.750 --> 03:33.980
Kyouka-chan, have you dealt 
with the guards outside?

03:34.320 --> 03:36.720
Demon Snow knocked them out.

03:38.920 --> 03:41.890
Mushitaro-san, let's escape together.

03:41.890 --> 03:43.010
I refuse.

03:43.800 --> 03:47.830
You just want me for my knowledge
 of the Decay of Angels, don't you?

03:47.830 --> 03:50.610
But I have no need for you lot.

03:50.610 --> 03:51.890
But...

03:51.890 --> 03:53.870
Don't you want to leave?

03:53.870 --> 03:56.080
I'm used to being locked up.

03:56.520 --> 04:01.260
Besides, there's nothing for me
 in the outside world anymore.

04:01.870 --> 04:05.100
Even if I leave, he's not...

04:06.000 --> 04:07.050
The manuscript.

04:08.620 --> 04:12.740
Rampo-san told me that you wouldn't 
be able to resist that word.

04:13.350 --> 04:17.060
It's enough to publicize the 
truth behind this manuscript.

04:18.940 --> 04:20.360
Is that a threat?

04:20.920 --> 04:24.750
You've become a true criminal 
organization now, haven't you?

04:25.200 --> 04:27.040
That may be.

04:27.350 --> 04:32.280
I'll become anything, if it's to 
save the Armed Detective Agency.

04:34.860 --> 04:40.100
Then you're aware that what you're doing 
right now is tantamount to bank robbery.

04:41.070 --> 04:43.620
We're inside a government bank.

04:43.620 --> 04:45.680
Breaking in, by itself, is a serious crime.

04:48.240 --> 04:49.590
Ah, whatever.

04:50.570 --> 04:52.340
I'll do as you say.

04:53.030 --> 04:54.560
You will?!

04:54.560 --> 04:56.070
Thank you!

04:58.690 --> 05:00.400
The escape route is this way.

05:01.460 --> 05:03.560
<i>The manuscript?!</i>

05:06.310 --> 05:10.440
<i>That was the last remnant of Yokomizo's life,
 that he entrusted me with.</i>

05:11.170 --> 05:13.540
<i>How dare they use it against me!</i>

05:14.060 --> 05:15.450
<i>Wretched bastards!</i>

05:17.770 --> 05:20.240
<i>I ought to let the guards take them.</i>

05:21.230 --> 05:23.950
<i>To that end, I need to make 
us as noticeable as we can.</i>

05:25.090 --> 05:27.430
My tummy hurts!

05:27.690 --> 05:28.820
Are you all right?

05:28.820 --> 05:29.880
Not at all!

05:29.880 --> 05:32.400
I might be a goner!

05:33.920 --> 05:35.170
Fine.

05:36.010 --> 05:38.590
I know of an acupuncture point 
that works on stomach pain.

05:38.590 --> 05:42.040
All it takes is a good jab three 
centimeters above the hipbone.

05:42.040 --> 05:43.660
Oh, I'm all good!

05:44.180 --> 05:47.170
It works so well, you feel better 
before you even get jabbed!

05:47.170 --> 05:47.950
Thanks.

05:48.710 --> 05:49.950
<i>You brat!</i>

05:50.320 --> 05:51.680
<i>I'm not done yet.</i>

05:51.680 --> 05:53.210
This is bad!

05:53.210 --> 05:56.900
This hallway is aligned with 
the Kabbalistic Taurus!

05:56.900 --> 05:59.260
Do not tread this evil path,
 you foolish normies!

05:59.540 --> 06:01.300
I know an acupuncture point 
that works on Kabbala.

06:01.300 --> 06:03.470
The alignment's all better!

06:03.740 --> 06:05.760
Such a powerful acupuncture point.

06:05.760 --> 06:06.670
Thanks.

06:07.970 --> 06:09.540
Yes, this is Group C.

06:10.010 --> 06:10.820
Yes.

06:10.820 --> 06:11.440
Yes.

06:11.730 --> 06:12.490
Understood.

06:12.490 --> 06:13.680
On our way.

06:15.150 --> 06:16.460
What's wrong?

06:16.460 --> 06:18.140
The guards are leaving.

06:21.160 --> 06:22.060
What the...

06:22.370 --> 06:24.990
P-Please, no, detective.

06:24.990 --> 06:26.510
Manager, sir...

06:27.280 --> 06:30.620
There is a wanted man 
hiding in this building.

06:30.930 --> 06:35.740
Please cease operations and 
grant us security authority.

06:36.390 --> 06:38.420
<i>The bank has been surrounded.</i>

06:38.770 --> 06:39.890
Good.

06:39.890 --> 06:41.800
We've assessed the
 targets' special abilities.

06:42.690 --> 06:44.170
We're hunting them down with all our might.

06:45.540 --> 06:46.640
What's the problem?

06:46.970 --> 06:49.190
The Special Operations 
Division has us surrounded.

06:49.800 --> 06:50.590
It's him!

06:52.550 --> 06:53.610
Shit...

06:53.610 --> 06:54.970
Ohh, shit.

06:54.970 --> 06:56.350
Why is <i>he</i> here?

06:56.790 --> 06:58.100
What is it?

06:58.100 --> 06:59.910
Sakaguchi Ango.

07:00.540 --> 07:03.640
If that man catches us, we're all done for.

07:06.350 --> 07:09.320
Are you aware of an organization 
called The Seventh Agency?

07:09.660 --> 07:13.210
They specialize in cleaning up 
crime and engaging in cover-ups.

07:13.910 --> 07:15.230
I've heard of it.

07:15.580 --> 07:18.190
That Fyodor rescued you from confinement

07:18.190 --> 07:21.910
and demanded cooperation during 
the Cannibalism in return.

07:22.160 --> 07:26.150
Sakaguchi Ango is the leader 
of that crime organization.

07:27.580 --> 07:28.760
That's impossible!

07:28.760 --> 07:30.830
Ango-san works for the government!

07:30.830 --> 07:32.570
Do you still not understand?

07:32.570 --> 07:35.580
The government created 
a crime organization!

07:36.820 --> 07:39.590
The Seventh Agency is the 
government's shadow.

07:39.590 --> 07:43.850
Cover-ups of political crimes, using illegal 
tactics, removing damaging rumors...

07:43.850 --> 07:45.630
I was the one who was given documents

07:45.630 --> 07:47.980
on all these things, 
so I could delete the evidence.

07:48.860 --> 07:53.550
There's no doubt that if we're captured, 
I'll be held until the day I die,

07:54.040 --> 07:56.090
and you two will be erased.

07:56.090 --> 07:58.740
If that's true, this trap will be brutal.

07:59.220 --> 08:01.300
The team within the 
Special Operations Division

08:01.300 --> 08:04.500
focuses on dealing with Gifted. 
Even the Port Mafia fears them.

08:04.800 --> 08:08.520
If we're found, they'll bombard us with poison gas
 and explosives and that will be checkmate.

08:08.520 --> 08:11.480
So we just need to avoid being found.

08:13.670 --> 08:16.100
Who do you think I am?

08:20.690 --> 08:22.550
Walk with pride!

08:26.490 --> 08:27.670
What's wrong?

08:27.670 --> 08:29.120
No, nothing.

08:29.120 --> 08:30.490
Impressed?

08:30.490 --> 08:34.820
If we walk around with stolen goods and use 
my special ability to erase evidence of crime,

08:35.210 --> 08:39.080
we vanish from any kind 
of surveillance video.

08:39.080 --> 08:40.120
Wow...

08:40.460 --> 08:43.600
<i>No wonder Rampo-san struggled 
against this ability.</i>

08:45.690 --> 08:47.130
Kyouka-chan, hide!

08:57.400 --> 09:00.260
The target is in this area.

09:00.890 --> 09:03.970
There are Gifted who can 
dismantle walls and ceilings.

09:04.500 --> 09:06.570
Secure the perimeter with caution.

09:08.210 --> 09:09.600
It's Ango-san.

09:09.600 --> 09:10.640
But why?

09:10.640 --> 09:13.110
My ability is perfect!

09:13.620 --> 09:14.840
This is bad.

09:14.840 --> 09:18.370
The hallway ahead is a 
dead end filled with vaults.

09:18.800 --> 09:19.870
There's nowhere to run.

09:20.270 --> 09:22.450
Could we hide in a vault?

09:22.450 --> 09:23.890
That's too dangerous.

09:23.890 --> 09:25.360
We'd be trapped like rats.

09:28.030 --> 09:29.120
They're coming!

09:30.090 --> 09:31.680
<i>There's no time.</i>

09:31.680 --> 09:33.380
<i>If they find us, we're doomed.</i>

09:33.380 --> 09:34.350
<i>What do we do?!</i>

09:36.100 --> 09:38.260
It's like you're trapped in a room.

09:39.670 --> 09:41.920
A trap without an exit.

09:41.920 --> 09:43.560
Just like a locked room.

09:44.040 --> 09:49.060
It'd make for an entertaining mystery 
if the criminal vanished from here.

09:49.430 --> 09:52.350
Don't you agree, Mushi-kun?

10:00.000 --> 10:01.150
You two.

10:03.370 --> 10:07.000
<b>Episode 48</b>

10:03.370 --> 10:07.000
<b>Jailbreak</b>

10:03.720 --> 10:04.950
Come with me.

10:11.780 --> 10:13.050
Target acquired!

10:13.050 --> 10:14.780
He's escaping into a vault!

10:16.950 --> 10:18.220
Neutralize the enemy!

10:18.620 --> 10:19.970
Gifted Combat Squad, advance!

10:22.930 --> 10:24.260
Explosives planted.

10:24.260 --> 10:26.400
Breach charges set.

10:26.660 --> 10:27.600
Detonate!

10:32.940 --> 10:33.960
Breach!

10:36.960 --> 10:39.070
Command, there's no one here.

10:39.490 --> 10:40.870
The target has vanished.

10:42.050 --> 10:42.980
What?!

10:50.330 --> 10:53.410
There's no sign that they've dug 
through the walls or ground.

10:53.830 --> 10:58.350
There isn't even a sign that 
they've used special abilities.

10:58.860 --> 11:00.960
They've vanished without a trace.

11:03.250 --> 11:04.590
See that, Special Operations?!

11:06.890 --> 11:08.110
Are you okay?

11:08.310 --> 11:09.710
That was nothing.

11:09.710 --> 11:12.240
Just the classic vanishing act.

11:12.670 --> 11:16.400
What they saw was the moment 
Demon Snow closed the vault door.

11:16.720 --> 11:20.680
We were, in fact, hiding in an 
open vault closer to the exit.

11:20.680 --> 11:22.230
And, in the moment of the attack,

11:22.230 --> 11:25.000
Kyouka-chan released 
Demon Snow and we escaped.

11:25.280 --> 11:28.960
It's psychological trickery,
 taking advantage of the expectation

11:28.960 --> 11:32.000
that we wouldn't be hiding in an open vault.

11:32.000 --> 11:34.200
The smarter you are, 
the more likely you are to fall for it.

11:34.200 --> 11:37.930
I'm amazed that you came up with 
that idea under so much pressure.

11:37.930 --> 11:42.410
Oh, no, I didn't come up with it.

11:43.260 --> 11:45.390
Someone taught me it a long time ago.

11:46.260 --> 11:47.380
Who did?

11:49.820 --> 11:51.980
Hide in the room next door?!

11:51.980 --> 11:55.220
Would that even count as a trick?

11:57.470 --> 12:00.320
You couldn't figure it out, though,
 could you, Mushi-kun?

12:02.660 --> 12:07.030
<b>We debated thousands
 upon thousands of times</b>

12:03.010 --> 12:05.070
<i>We debated thousands upon 
thousands of times.</i>

12:04.490 --> 12:07.030
<b>It seeped into the very fiber of my being.</b>

12:05.070 --> 12:07.020
<i>It seeped into the very fiber of my being.</i>

12:09.060 --> 12:10.270
<i>Yokomizo...</i>

12:10.870 --> 12:13.210
<i>Were you always there?</i>

12:14.480 --> 12:18.240
Can I always meet you in a closed room?

12:19.150 --> 12:23.010
Life seems exciting and fun 
around you these days.

12:23.820 --> 12:28.420
Better for your well-being than writing 
those dull letters, I'd say.

12:29.780 --> 12:32.110
Shut up, you sell-out.

12:33.480 --> 12:34.860
Mushitaro-san?

12:35.170 --> 12:37.780
Now, we just need to steal a car and run.

12:38.230 --> 12:43.120
First, we erase the evidence of 
having stolen a car using my ability.

12:43.490 --> 12:49.380
That way, the city security camera footage 
and stolen car police documents vanish.

12:50.580 --> 12:52.610
You sure are something else.

12:52.900 --> 12:57.740
This sewer line will take us to a 
parking lot away from the guards.

12:57.740 --> 12:59.110
I'll handle it.

13:03.760 --> 13:05.940
I'll go in first and check—

13:09.780 --> 13:10.700
Hey!

13:14.820 --> 13:15.650
<i>A dummy grenade!</i>

13:18.400 --> 13:19.660
Unacceptable.

13:20.510 --> 13:23.600
I can't have you thinking you 
can deceive me that easily.

13:24.250 --> 13:24.960
Impossible!

13:24.960 --> 13:25.690
How did you find us here?

13:25.990 --> 13:28.540
Ango-san, please, listen.

13:28.540 --> 13:31.550
The Detective Agency is innocent.

13:31.550 --> 13:33.580
The real enemy is elsewhere.

13:33.880 --> 13:36.050
I trust you to understand.

13:36.050 --> 13:37.070
Believe me!

13:38.790 --> 13:40.300
You're right.

13:40.300 --> 13:41.940
I understand.

13:43.350 --> 13:50.010
My special ability allows me to extract 
memories residing in objects.

13:51.310 --> 13:54.350
I used this to determine your escape route.

13:55.440 --> 13:58.270
I used this ability to learn 
everything about the crime scene.

13:58.700 --> 14:02.200
Therefore, I can be certain the 
Detective Agency is guilty.

14:02.510 --> 14:04.410
You also stabbed Chief Taneda!

14:05.840 --> 14:12.150
Rampo-san said the government has 
a Gifted who can read memories.

14:13.180 --> 14:17.170
He also said that if we're captured, 
we're bound to be executed.

14:18.240 --> 14:21.660
You would honestly beg a secret government 
organization to just believe you?

14:22.030 --> 14:24.710
The Agency's jokes have never 
been funny, to the very end.

14:25.680 --> 14:28.690
<i>I underestimated the 
Special Operations Division.</i>

14:49.110 --> 14:50.860
Commander, where are the targets?

14:51.330 --> 14:52.450
They got away.

14:53.060 --> 14:54.820
They escaped through the manhole.

14:54.820 --> 14:58.670
They're using the tiger's 
special ability to head west.

14:59.590 --> 15:01.340
Secure the area!

15:01.340 --> 15:02.230
Yes, sir.

15:04.150 --> 15:08.510
This will convince Fyodor 
that we are enemies.

15:09.100 --> 15:13.860
You believe me that the 
Detective Agency is innocent?

15:13.860 --> 15:19.390
You saw a message from Dazai-kun 
in Francis' office, correct?

15:20.930 --> 15:23.440
I was the one who sent that message.

15:23.440 --> 15:24.140
Huh?

15:24.560 --> 15:25.560
So, then...

15:26.070 --> 15:29.370
Dazai-kun and I have been 
cooperating since the beginning.

15:30.090 --> 15:33.280
I am Dazai-kun's messenger 
while he is confined.

15:33.920 --> 15:37.110
But how is Dazai-san communicating 
with the outside?

15:37.420 --> 15:40.690
Prisoners at the Mersault detention center

15:40.690 --> 15:43.290
are implanted with a vital sign monitor
 in order to prevent escape.

15:43.780 --> 15:48.580
Dazai-kun encodes his 
messages in his heart rate,

15:48.580 --> 15:52.410
which I then use my government 
access to retrieve and decode.

15:53.030 --> 15:55.810
He's controlling his own heart rate?

15:56.280 --> 15:58.910
It's a very Dazai-kun party trick.

15:58.910 --> 16:00.630
No one would suspect a thing.

16:00.630 --> 16:02.470
I don't believe you.

16:02.470 --> 16:03.980
You're an enemy.

16:04.360 --> 16:07.540
What was the point of that charade, anyway?

16:07.920 --> 16:10.360
There's no telling where Fyodor has eyes.

16:10.950 --> 16:16.990
With my ability to read memories, 
I can pursue any escapee.

16:17.680 --> 16:20.490
If I were to just lose you, 
the enemy would be suspicious.

16:20.490 --> 16:21.480
The enemy?

16:22.690 --> 16:26.180
The cunning Seventh Agency 
is afraid of the enemy?

16:26.180 --> 16:28.180
That's the thing, Mushitaro-san.

16:29.400 --> 16:34.050
So it's true that you've been told 
 I'm with the Seventh Agency.

16:34.050 --> 16:35.730
What if I have?

16:35.730 --> 16:36.840
It's simple.

16:37.720 --> 16:40.860
I'm not with the Seventh Agency.

16:41.140 --> 16:42.320
What?

16:42.320 --> 16:43.980
Fyodor lied.

16:44.710 --> 16:47.080
To keep you away from me.

16:48.280 --> 16:53.350
That's how afraid he is of 
us talking to each other.

16:54.500 --> 16:57.760
Let's continue this
 conversation where it's safe.

16:58.900 --> 17:00.300
Are you serious?!

17:00.300 --> 17:01.640
What's wrong with you?!

17:01.640 --> 17:04.280
What do you mean you're <i>wanted?!</i>

17:04.280 --> 17:05.940
Ow, ow...

17:05.220 --> 17:07.390
Is this place really safe?

17:07.390 --> 17:10.880
Only those she invites can enter.

17:10.880 --> 17:12.460
It's the safest place on earth.

17:12.730 --> 17:16.220
Wait, Lucy-chan. Why are 
you even with Ango-san?

17:17.100 --> 17:18.510
Well, that's...

17:18.510 --> 17:19.880
Not for any particular reason.

17:19.880 --> 17:21.080
I'm protecting her.

17:21.080 --> 17:21.590
Hey!

17:21.920 --> 17:25.270
She barged into the 
investigation headquarters.

17:25.840 --> 17:31.070
"Atsushi-kun's not evil. There's no way 
he's a murderer," she said, maniacally.

17:31.070 --> 17:32.530
Stop it!

17:32.530 --> 17:34.230
Don't tell him!

17:34.730 --> 17:36.670
Wow, that's kind of you.

17:36.670 --> 17:38.360
Thank you, Lucy-chan.

17:39.250 --> 17:41.700
Never mind that. Tell me, Sakaguchi Ango...

17:42.130 --> 17:47.510
I was once captured by an organization that 
forced me to help cover up their crimes.

17:48.590 --> 17:52.600
That evil organization was 
called the Seventh Agency.

17:53.470 --> 17:57.690
Are you truly not with that organization?

17:57.690 --> 17:58.210
I am not.

17:59.190 --> 18:02.930
Have you ever made use of their services?

18:07.710 --> 18:08.690
I have.

18:13.130 --> 18:16.690
Then I have no reason to cooperate with you.

18:17.660 --> 18:19.730
But only once.

18:23.320 --> 18:24.620
Four years ago.

18:24.620 --> 18:27.670
To make sure Dazai-kun could 
live outside the Port Mafia.

18:27.970 --> 18:30.110
I erased his past crimes.

18:33.010 --> 18:36.270
Why did you dirty your hands just that once?

18:47.350 --> 18:52.230
A desperate attempt to make
 amends for a friend long gone.

18:56.850 --> 19:00.640
For a friend long gone, huh?

19:01.200 --> 19:04.320
Mushitaro-san, you're correct.

19:04.320 --> 19:06.440
The Seventh Agency is evil.

19:06.440 --> 19:09.490
Their scope, their members, 
their hierarchy...

19:09.490 --> 19:10.670
Everything is unknown.

19:11.090 --> 19:13.840
Even I had to go through 
four levels of middlemen

19:13.840 --> 19:16.950
to work with that government 
crime organization.

19:17.300 --> 19:18.870
I see.

19:18.870 --> 19:22.010
So that's why you work independently.

19:22.480 --> 19:23.250
Yes.

19:24.020 --> 19:25.390
What's going on?

19:26.040 --> 19:30.360
This man suspects there's a 
spy inside the government.

19:32.780 --> 19:34.490
I can't trust anyone.

19:34.960 --> 19:38.550
I'm the only one who can 
avenge Chief Taneda.

19:39.050 --> 19:42.870
To that end, I need to hear what you know.

19:43.290 --> 19:46.020
The knowledge that Fyodor tried 
so hard to hide from me.

19:46.910 --> 19:48.960
I ask on his behalf, as well.

19:48.960 --> 19:51.970
I know you have no reason to tell us.

19:52.500 --> 19:53.870
Please.

19:56.580 --> 19:58.250
Where do I start?

19:59.170 --> 20:02.730
But, just so you know, in five 
minutes you'll be regretting it.

20:03.360 --> 20:08.160
Anything you ask, all of my answers 
will absolutely ruin your day.

20:08.160 --> 20:11.050
Most important question first, then.

20:11.740 --> 20:15.150
What is the Decay of Angels?

20:15.380 --> 20:20.370
The terrorist organization, Decay of Angels,
 is comprised of five members.

20:20.370 --> 20:23.300
The demonic Fyodor and jester Nikolai,

20:23.300 --> 20:25.280
as well as two more extremely 
talented Gifted.

20:25.840 --> 20:29.950
And one founder who manages them.

20:30.170 --> 20:32.370
Someone <i>above</i> Fyodor?

20:32.940 --> 20:35.250
I don't know what their ultimate goal is.

20:35.660 --> 20:38.840
But I do know what their current plan is,
 just one step ahead of it.

20:40.050 --> 20:41.720
The erasure of the state.

20:41.720 --> 20:43.470
Erasure?

20:43.470 --> 20:44.930
Not an overturning?

20:46.330 --> 20:47.740
That's absurd!

20:47.740 --> 20:49.180
They could never pull it off!

20:49.420 --> 20:51.300
They have the page.

20:52.350 --> 20:54.620
But there's only one page.

20:54.620 --> 20:57.620
They used it when they framed the Agency.

20:57.830 --> 21:00.600
They can use it just once more.

21:01.130 --> 21:02.230
Right.

21:02.230 --> 21:03.490
There's still the other side.

21:03.990 --> 21:05.100
That's right.

21:05.470 --> 21:10.880
The page is activated 
the moment it's written upon,

21:10.880 --> 21:14.820
and the page is blank on both sides.

21:15.570 --> 21:17.840
In other words, they're keeping 
the other side ready,

21:18.510 --> 21:22.910
so they have the power 
to recreate that tragedy.

21:23.250 --> 21:25.820
Why don't they use it right away, then?

21:26.450 --> 21:34.030
For the page to be activated, it needs to 
have a narrative-like causal consistency.

21:34.690 --> 21:35.740
Correct?

21:35.740 --> 21:36.570
That's right.

21:36.570 --> 21:42.410
And because of that rule, a grand conspiracy 
necessarily requires a lot of text.

21:42.810 --> 21:46.130
So they'll only write the 
important details onto the page,

21:46.130 --> 21:50.000
and will deal with the 
trivial details themselves.

21:50.000 --> 21:51.610
That's the current phase of their plan.

21:51.980 --> 21:54.900
Next, they'll engage in global terrorism.

21:54.900 --> 21:59.410
Then, as the final phase of their plan,
 they'll use the last page.

21:59.800 --> 22:03.010
And the state will be erased. Is that it?

22:04.640 --> 22:09.550
The other side of the page will be written 
on the night of the next full moon.

22:15.280 --> 22:16.870
Ten days from now.

22:18.540 --> 22:19.640
Shit.

22:20.300 --> 22:23.570
You're right. I feel like garbage, 
having heard that.

22:29.480 --> 22:34.730
I will escort you and relay 
this information to Dazai-kun.

22:42.280 --> 22:44.350
Hey, will you be all right?

22:46.080 --> 22:47.290
Yes!

22:47.750 --> 22:49.820
We did it, Kyouka-chan!

22:49.820 --> 22:50.970
Huh?

22:50.970 --> 22:53.010
Wh-What's gotten into you?

22:53.570 --> 22:55.930
Ten days until the other side 
of the page is written.

22:56.460 --> 22:58.840
In other words, they can't 
write anything until then.

22:59.250 --> 23:00.270
Right.

23:00.270 --> 23:04.860
It'll take at least ten days 
to prepare the final step.

23:06.520 --> 23:10.640
The Detective Agency's been made criminals 
because of the page's reality-altering effect.

23:10.640 --> 23:13.100
We can't undo that...

23:13.100 --> 23:14.500
Or so I thought.

23:15.110 --> 23:16.490
But that's not true.

23:17.250 --> 23:21.120
We'll take the page back and write 
that the Agency is innocent.

23:21.120 --> 23:22.580
That'll fix everything.

23:22.580 --> 23:26.390
We track down the Decay of Angels 
within ten days and defeat them,

23:26.760 --> 23:27.960
and take the page back.

23:28.170 --> 23:29.590
That's it.

23:29.590 --> 23:31.020
That's all we need to do.

23:31.820 --> 23:33.930
Let's do it, Kyouka-chan!

23:35.350 --> 23:37.010
There's still hope.

23:37.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode: 49

23:37.020 --> 23:40.010
<i>Bungo Hound Dogs</i>
